## Defense-in-depth against agent workspace-leak bugs:
## the VDT runner repo should ONLY contain VirtualDevTeam.* projects under src/.
## Anything else under src/ is almost certainly an agent leak (see GridGuardians.Api
## incident 2026-05-11 where target-project files landed at src/GridGuardians.Api/).
## If the leak is intentional (e.g. you're committing a new VDT sub-project), edit
## this rule and add an explicit !src/YourProject/ allowlist entry.
/src/*
!/src/VirtualDevTeam.*/

## Playwright MCP snapshots (generated during test/evaluation runs)
.playwright-mcp/
**/.playwright-mcp/

runner.out
runner.err
reset.err
reset.log

# Working/local recommendations doc — not for commit
docs/ImproveEngPrompts.md


# Temp bootstrap workspace (used for ad-hoc tests, e.g. mcp-validation, render-test).
# Entire directory is operator-local — was tracked by mistake in the initial AgentSquad
# import 2026-05-01, cleaned up 2026-05-11 per the workspace-leak audit.
temp_bootstrap/


# FixRecommendation plans + state — operator-local, generated at runtime, not shared
FixRecommendations/

# ReadMe authoring artifacts — entire directory is operator-local until the workflow stabilises.
# The capture-screenshots.mjs/.ps1 scripts + generated images live here; nothing here ships to others.
# Re-share specific files (e.g. capture script) by removing or scoping this rule when ready.
ReadMe/

# === Don't-Affect-Others plan (2026-05-11) ===
# Per-developer preview-build config (contains absolute clone path).
# Copy preview-settings.template.json → preview-settings.json on first run.
preview-settings.json

# Runtime-mutated SME agent definitions registry.
# Copy sme-definitions.template.json → sme-definitions.json on first run, or let the runner create it on demand.
sme-definitions.json

# Node.js --report-on-fatalerror crash dumps (contains absolute paths + PIDs + command-line args).
# Naming pattern: report.<YYYYMMDD>.<HHMMSS>.<PID>.<seq>.json
report.[0-9]*.json

# MSAL / IdentityService token caches — credential artifacts, never commit
.IdentityService/

# Agent-generated documents accidentally dropped into the Runner working directory.
# (Long-term, these should be routed to .agents/ or a runner-output/ dir that's already gitignored.)
src/VirtualDevTeam.Runner/*-evaluation.md
src/VirtualDevTeam.Runner/*-research.md
src/VirtualDevTeam.Runner/*-report.md

# === Target project artifacts ===
# Agent-built target projects that leaked into the VDT repo root.
# These are output from pipeline runs, not VDT source code.
Compliance2/
Compliance2.Tests/

# Agent-generated tracking/documentation artifacts
AgentDocs/

# Temporary debug/audit scripts (one-off, not production tooling)
scripts-tmp/

# Python bytecode cache
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Root-level temp screenshots (use Screenshots/ for README-referenced images)
/*.png

# PowerShell null-redirect artifact
$null
